      "problem": "A t-shirt costs $\\[math]18$ before tax. If a $9\\%$ sales tax is applied, what is the total cost after tax?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the total cost after tax, we apply a $9\\%$ increase to the original price.\n\nIncreasing by $9\\%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100\\% + 9\\% = 109\\% = 1.09\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original price by $1.09{:}$\n\n$$\n18 \\times 1.09 = 19.62.\n$$\n\nSo, the total cost after tax is $\\[math]19.62.$",
